  "operation": {
    "kind": "prompt",
    "user": "Turn the issue into product deliverables: who is served, what they can do, and\nhow we would know it worked.\n\n## The issue\n\n{{.inputs.issue}}\n\n## The docs this phase reads\n\n{{.inputs.working_set}}\n\n**These are paths, not contents.** Open each one with `read_file` before you start. Read the\nfile as it is now — an earlier state in this phase may have edited it since the run began.\n\n\n## The framing this exploration chose\n\n{{.inputs.framing}}\n\n{{.inputs.residue}}\n\nIf those are empty, the catalog already answered the framing question and you\nshould work from the issue directly.\n\n## Answer these, in order\n\n1. **Who are we serving?** The user, a developer, support, marketing? Name one\n   per deliverable, and name them the way they would describe themselves.\n2. **What are the goals?** How does this bring value to that person? Can we\n   measure that value — what does success look like, and what does failure look\n   like?\n3. **How does this feature bring that value?** What is necessary, what is\n   sufficient, and what is merely nice to have?\n4. **What other features must exist** for this one to deliver its value?\n5. **Where does this sit among the features that already exist** — what does it\n   overlap with, what does it make redundant, and what would a user expect it to\n   do because of a neighbour?\n6. **Does it conform to the product principles?** If not, this is an *exception*\n   (with the reason, on the doc claiming it) or an *amendment* (the principle is\n   wrong). Silence is neither, and phase 8 finds silent departures.\n\n## What to produce\n\n`features` — one entry per deliverable:\n\n```\n{ \"id\": \"feature-name\",\n  \"story\": \"As a [who], I should be able to [what] so that I can [value]\",\n  \"importance\": 0.0-1.0,\n  \"metrics\": [\"...\"],\n  \"requires\": [\"other-feature-name\"] }\n```\n\nTwo things to get right in the story. The **who** has to be someone who would\nrecognise this as their job. The **so that I can** has to name something the\nperson wanted *before this feature existed* — \"so that I can use the new panel\"\nis the feature wearing a story's clothes.\n\nThe metrics must measure the **value**, not the activity. Opens, clicks and\nruns-started measure that the feature was reached. Ask which metric would move\nif the feature were popular and useless, and do not write that one.\n\n`feature_docs` — one doc per deliverable, on the `docs/_templates/product-feature.md`\ntemplate. Each carries its upward link, a **Where this fits** section (serves /\nneighbors / depends on / history), and — where the exploration rejected a\nreading — a **Framings considered** row.\n\n`standing_amendment` — only when `product/principles.md` is itself wrong. The\ngate approves an amendment separately from the feature, so do not fold one into\na doc.\n",
    "config": {
      "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5"
    },
    "input": {},
    "output": {
      "name": "output",
      "kind": "json",
      "schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "features": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "object",
              "required": [
                "id",
                "story",
                "importance",
                "metrics"
              ],
              "properties": {
                "id": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "story": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "description": "As a [who], I should be able to [what] so that I can [value]."
                },
                "importance": {
                  "type": "number",
                  "minimum": 0,
                  "maximum": 1
                },
                "metrics": {
                  "type": "array",
                  "items": {
                    "type": "string"
                  }
                },
                "requires": {
                  "type": "array",
                  "items": {
                    "type": "string"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "feature_docs": {
            "type": "string",
            "contentMediaType": "text/markdown"
          },
          "standing_amendment": {
            "type": "string",
            "contentMediaType": "text/markdown"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "features",
          "feature_docs"
        ]
      }
    }
  },
  "environment": {
    "tools": [
      "read_file"
    ]
  },
  "slotMeta": {
    "inputs.issue": {
      "description": "What is being asked for."
    },
    "inputs.framing": {
      "optional": true,
      "description": "The winning framing from the exploration. Absent when the catalog already answered it."
    },
    "inputs.residue": {
      "optional": true,
      "description": "What the exploration leaves behind — the Framings considered rows."
    },
    "inputs.working_set": {
      "optional": true,
      "description": "Paths to the docs this phase reads — its standing docs and the catalog entries that bear on the feature. Open them with read_file: the file as it is now, not a copy taken before this phase started editing."
    },
    "outputs.standing_amendment": {
      "optional": true
    }
  }
}
